# Topic permissions for the cloud-profile broker (backend/mosquitto/mosquitto.tls.conf).
# PURPOSE: Least privilege per identity. The "user" below is the CN of the client certificate (tools/pki.sh), not a password login.
# HOW: One stanza per identity; no "#" grants anywhere. Topics: ehg/<node>/pkt = packets, ehg/_gw/<gateway>/status = online/offline.
#   A gateway can publish packets and its OWN status only. Readers cannot publish. To add a gateway: tools/pki.sh client ehg-gw-02,
#   then copy the ehg-gw-01 stanza with the new name (both lines). Mosquitto re-reads this file on SIGHUP or restart.
# KNOWN LIMIT: "ehg/+/pkt" lets a gateway publish packets for ANY node id; it cannot be pinned to the nodes it serves without a node list.
# ROLE IN THESIS: Access control on the gateway-to-broker boundary (docs/decisions/0008-mqtt-mtls-and-topic-acls.md).
# BEFORE -> AFTER: Before: anyone could publish or read everything. After: see the stanzas.

user ehg-gw-01
topic write ehg/+/pkt
topic write ehg/_gw/ehg-gw-01/status

user ehg-bridge
topic read ehg/+/pkt
topic read ehg/_gw/+/status

user ehg-ingest
topic read ehg/+/pkt

user ehg-viewer
topic read ehg/+/pkt
